,"unstructured":"We generated random d-regular graphs up to d=min(30,N\u22121). This covered all values of N, d run for both MB and XEB. For the deeper transport 1Q RB sequences, circuit layers were repeated cyclically after reaching the maximum d=30.","type":"other"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc38R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1016\/S0375-9601(02)01272-0","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc39R1","unstructured":"Strictly speaking, leakage errors should be subtracted out from the average fidelity data prior to conversion to process fidelities and then added back in as a process error. Estimate of our leakage rates from both 2Q RB and transport 1Q RB suggest an aggregate leakage probability of 7(2)\u00d710\u22124 per 2Q gate. As this rate is small compared to the quoted process error per 2Q gate of 3.2(1)\u00d710\u22123, we expect such corrections to be very small.","type":"other"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc42R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/s41534-019-0196-1","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc43R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.21468\/SciPostPhys.7.5.060","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc44R1","volume-title":"Proceedings of the International Conference for High Performance Computing, Networking, Storage and Analysis","author":"S. Atchley","year":"2023","type":"conference-proceedings"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc46R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevLett.71.1291","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc47R1","unstructured":"This point has been the source of some debate in the literature; see the appendixes for further discussion.","type":"other"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc48R1","volume-title":"Proceedings of the 2016 Meeting on Algorithm Engineering and Experiments (ALENEX)","author":"S. Schlag","type":"conference-proceedings"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc49R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","volume-title":"Proceedings of the 2017 Meeting on Algorithm Engineering and Experiments (ALENEX)","author":"Y. Akhremtsev","DOI":"10.1137\/1.9781611974768.3","type":"conference-proceedings"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc50R1","unstructured":"It is important to note that actually computing FXEBlin classically from the quantum data is expected to be infeasible classically in the regime that RCS is classically hard, so the specific notion of verifiability discussed here applies to the ability to verify the data in principle and not in practice.","type":"other"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc51R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevLett.119.180509","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc52R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevLett.130.173202","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc54R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/s41567-018-0124-x","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc55R1","volume-title":"Proceedings of the 55th Annual ACM Symposium on Theory of Computing, STOC 2023","author":"D. Aharonov","year":"2023","type":"conference-proceedings"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc56R1","unstructured":"It is worth noting that the classical approach to RCS used to show N-asymptotic easiness at fixed noise rate in Ref.\u00a0[55] scales exponentially with the inverse of the gate error rate, leaving open the possibility that the window of system sizes controlled by noiseless asymptotics may be quite large even at modest gate error rates.","type":"other"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc57R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1103\/PhysRevLett.129.130501","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc58R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1038\/s41467-019-13068-7","type":"journal-article"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc59R1","volume-title":"Mathematics of statistics","author":"J. Kenney","year":"1951","type":"book"},{"key":"PhysRevX.15.021052Cc60R1","doi-asserted-by":"publisher","DOI":"10.1017\/S0963548300001735","ty